Subject: [PATCH 11253/11362] Record reviewer findings 3-5 and the lesson from
 finding 4

Finding 4 is the one worth keeping past this branch. The round-three agent
reported "15/15 mutations RED, none survived" and that statement is true: every
mutation it wrote bit a real assertion. Two producer writes simply had no mutation
written for them, and the reviewer proved it by deleting them and watching the
suite stay green.

A proof table showing N of N RED says nothing about code no mutation was ever
written for. A missing mutation and a surviving mutation have the same
consequence, and only the second is visible in the table. The completeness
question -- which producer writes are named by no mutation -- has to be asked
separately.

Also records that cd82's non-monotone level counter is now corroborated here from
the artifact (a segment completing level 1 behind a final counter of 0), and that
finding 3 predates this branch so the agent is not told it caused it.

