+### Findings 3 to 5, and the cd82 corroboration (13:40Z)
+
+**cd82 non-monotone counter — NOW CORROBORATED HERE, independently of the reviewer.**
+`results/arc_leaderboard_eval_runs/cd82-r11l-727651.json` `per_game[1]` reads final `levels: 0`
+and `deepest_level_reached: 0`, while `level_reset_attribution.segments` holds one segment with
+`level_completed: 1`. A completed level behind a final counter of zero is a non-monotone counter,
+which is all finding 1 requires. The exact indices `(770, 0->1) (873, 1->0) (1512, 0->1)
+(1615, 1->0)` remain the reviewer's; I did not reconstruct them.
+
+**Finding 4 — the one that changes how this round is reported. Two producer fields are bitten by
+NO mutation.** `experiment_6921_arc_dynamic_supervisor_banked_credit.py:721-734` passes
+`arms_enabled`, `unredirected_windows` and `unredirected_windows_dropped` into the corrected
+ledger. Only `unredirected_windows` is covered (M9). The reviewer deleted the other two and the
+suite stayed green, because the single test exercising the path
+(`test_req_arc_wmte_6921_new_arm_receipt_stays_recommendation_only`) uses a fixture with all four
+arms in `redirects`, so `enabled_arms_for_entry` returns the same set via the `legacy_default`
+fallback whether or not `arms_enabled` survives — and the test asserts only `cells[0]["level"]`.
+
+**The lesson, and it generalises past this branch.** The agent reported "15/15 mutations RED,
+none survived." That statement is TRUE. Every mutation it wrote bit a real assertion. Two
+producer writes simply had no mutation written for them. **A proof table showing N of N RED says
+nothing about code that no mutation was ever written for** — a missing mutation and a surviving
+mutation have the same consequence and only the second is visible in the table. The completeness
+question has to be asked separately: which producer writes are not named by any mutation?
+Reviewer's fix: assert `arms_enabled_source == "receipt"` and add a `dropped > 0` fixture, then
+add the two matching mutations.
+
+**Finding 3, full text now received, reviewer's, not verified here.** `enabled <= arms_used`
+tests whether every enabled arm was SPENT. It cannot express a window where the arms are unspent
+but every one is INELIGIBLE — `attempt_cap_reached` blocks both re-induction rungs,
+`goal_bias_installed: False` blocks `drop_goal_bias`. Such a window is neither a cell nor
+not-decidable, while the report tells the reader zero cells means no level ran dry. The reviewer
+quotes REQ-7031's own Origin paragraph describing exactly this state on `r11l-1594772` level 2.
+**This PREDATES the branch** — inherited from REQ-6640/7030's framing; the branch's contribution
+is the over-claiming sentence. Computable from fields the 7031 rows already carry.
+
+**Finding 5, MINOR, reviewer's, truncated — remainder requested.** `stagnations_unredirected`
+enters `base` and rides onto every per-level cell while remaining a whole-run count;
+`windows_dropped` is the entry total, not the level's, and REQ-7033 rule 4 lists it among the
+per-cell fields without qualifying it. The 7033-C test cannot discriminate because all 64 of its
+rows are on level 2. In a change whose subject is not pooling, two pooled fields sit unqualified
+on a per-level record.
+
+**Routing:** all findings go to the agent that owns the file, not to the reviewer. A finding and
+the right to edit are separate things; putting the finder on the fix has already put two agents
+on one file three times today. DECISION 18 is unaffected and still open.
 
 
